Appendix: evidence, method and sources
Every number in this doc comes from running the project's own, unchanged code; only the LLM was replaced by a stub where noted.
How it was measured
• Engine runs: the project's stepWorldState() and apply*Result() functions, run headless for 3 to 7 sim days at the App's tick rate (100 ms ticks; at 1x, one sim minute per 0.65 s).
• Scheduler runs: a copy of the App's job-picking rules (one job in flight, 14 s between starts, same priority order) with a fake LLM taking 4 s per call. Also run at 2x and 5x, with a persistent failure, and with a 0.5 s model. The near-instant model gave the same conversation count, so the limit is the scheduler, not model speed.
• Full stack: the project's own smallvilleApi.ts calling its own Express server, with a stub in place of OpenRouter that recorded every prompt.
• Data checks: a validator over all residents, buildings, objects, doors and rumours.
• Tooling: a clean copy with the Phase 0 fixes applied. npm install (179 packages), lint and build succeed, and npm test passes 12 of 12. Reading the key from .env.local works with dotenv.config({ path: ['.env.local', '.env'] }).
• Not tested: how good the real model's writing is, real latency, and how often the default free model returns broken JSON.
